{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH your Elohim, etc.</b> There is a dispute among the commentators, for some say that only 'I am' and 'You shall have no other god' did we hear from the mouth of the Almighty, and their proof is from the fact that these two commandments were stated in the language of one speaking on his own behalf, while the rest of the commandments are in the language of the hidden. And some say that we heard all ten commandments from the mouth of the Holy One, blessed be He, and what they said (Exodus 20:19) 'You speak with us and we will hear' — this was after they heard the ten commandments. And according to this view, the matter requires explanation: why were specifically these two commandments stated in the language of one speaking on his own behalf?\n\nAnd according to its plain sense, the matter applies equally to both, for it is the way of the world that after a person sees the face of the king and recognizes him and knows him, from then on he accepts him as king. And after he has accepted upon himself the yoke of his kingship, it is fitting to accept his commandments, whether what he commands him through an emissary or what he commands him himself, even though he did not see the face of the king at the time of the command. But if he has never yet seen the face of the king and is in doubt about accepting him — how could he obey his emissary, for if there is no sender there is no emissary? So too the Holy One, blessed be He, needed to speak first in direct address, 'I am YHWH your Elohim,' to bring them into the covenant of accepting His divinity, for 'eye to eye they shall see' (Isaiah 52:8) YHWH His holy one. And after accepting His divinity, it is fitting to heed also His emissary who comes in His name.\n\nAnd indeed, since He said 'I am YHWH your Elohim who brought you out of the land of Egypt,' and did not say 'who created you' and 'who created heaven and earth' — for the reason that will be explained below — from this an argument emerged for those who err to say: if you tell us that this is so, that this is YHWH who brought us out of the land of Egypt — perhaps there is another god who created us and who created heaven and earth, and what did you see to heed the voice of this Elohim, our Elohim, who brought us out of Egypt? Perhaps there is another Elohim who created us, and whose voice we should hear. Therefore He said immediately, 'You shall have no other elohim before My face,' to teach that there is no god besides Him. And if so, you are not permitted to heed any emissary but only this emissary from Me.\n\n<parabreak>\n\nAnd according to its plain sense, the matter applies equally to both, for it is the way of the world that after a person sees the face of the king and recognizes him and knows him, from then on he accepts him as king. And after he has accepted upon himself the yoke of his kingship, it is fitting to accept his commandments, whether what he commands him through an emissary or what he commands him himself, even though he did not see the face of the king at the time of the command. But if he has never yet seen the face of the king and is in doubt about accepting him — how could he obey his emissary, for if there is no sender there is no emissary? So too the Holy One, blessed be He, needed to speak first in direct address, 'I am YHWH your Elohim,' to bring them into the covenant of accepting His divinity, for 'eye to eye they shall see' (Isaiah 52:8) YHWH His holy one. And after accepting His divinity, it is fitting to heed also His emissary who comes in His name.\n\nAnd indeed, since He said 'I am YHWH your Elohim who brought you out of the land of Egypt,' and did not say 'who created you' and 'who created heaven and earth' — for the reason that will be explained below — from this an argument emerged for those who err to say: if you tell us that this is so, that this is YHWH who brought us out of the land of Egypt — perhaps there is another god who created us and who created heaven and earth, and what did you see to heed the voice of this Elohim, our Elohim, who brought us out of Egypt? Perhaps there is another Elohim who created us, and whose voice we should hear. Therefore He said immediately, 'You shall have no other elohim before My face,' to teach that there is no god besides Him. And if so, you are not permitted to heed any emissary but only this emissary from Me." "And therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, needed to command these two commandments in direct address, in order to strengthen in their hearts acceptance of the yoke of the kingdom of heaven, and afterward they were automatically obligated to heed also His emissary who speaks in the language of the hidden. But He could not command these two commandments through an emissary, for they had not yet accepted upon themselves the Sender as god — and if there is no sender there is no emissary. And this resolution agrees with both opinions, for according to the opinion of those who say that 'I am' and 'You shall have no other god' they heard from the mouth of the Almighty, it works well, in order to inform them who is the Sender whose emissary's voice it is fitting to heed. And according to the opinion of those who say that all the commandments were heard from the mouth of the Almighty — behold, in the first two commandments YHWH spoke with them face to face in direct address, so that they would recognize who is their king, and after this they are obligated to heed His voice even if they see no form but the voice. Even though in the first ones too they saw no form, nevertheless direct speech indicates speech face to face, as it is written (Deuteronomy 5:4) 'Face to face did YHWH speak with you,' etc. But the rest of the commandments He spoke in the language of the hidden, to inform that He is a hiding El, and even so they are obligated to heed His voice after accepting the yoke of His kingship face to face." "Another matter: since all these commandments are obligations of the body and do not depend on the Land, and Israel is obligated in them both in the Land and outside the Land, both at a time when the Temple stands and at a time when it does not stand — except for these two commandments, 'I am' and 'You shall have no other god,' which are not fulfilled except at a time when Israel dwell on their soil and YHWH shines His face upon them and speaks with them in direct address, for they are not in a state of hiddenness of face. But at a time when the sons have been exiled from the table of their father, then 'I am YHWH your Elohim' is not fulfilled, for our Rabbis of blessed memory already said (Ketubot 110b) that one who dwells outside the Land is as though he has no Elohim, etc.; and 'You shall have no other elohim' is not fulfilled, for it is stated in the reproof (Deuteronomy 28:64) 'and you shall serve there other elohim.' Rashi explained: from the fact that you pay a tax to priests of idolatry, Scripture accounts it to you as though you served them — end of quote. The Holy One, blessed be He, spoke these two commandments specifically in direct address, for at a time when Israel are in their success it is said (Leviticus 26:9) 'and I will turn My face to you,' and then the Holy One, blessed be He, speaks with them face to face, and at that time these two commandments are fulfilled; therefore 'before My face' is stated. But the rest of the commandments are fulfilled even at a time when Israel are in hiddenness of face; therefore they are stated in the language of the hidden.\n\nAnd this is what they said (Makkot 24a): 'I am' and 'You shall have no other god' — from the mouth of the Almighty we heard them. They mentioned specifically the epithet 'Almighty' with respect to HaShem, blessed be He, for this was said concerning a time when Israel are in their tranquility, and at that time they add strength to the Attribute of above. But at a time when they are in hiddenness of face, they weaken His strength, as it were, as our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Yalkut Ha'azinu, 945) that the righteous add strength to the Attribute of above, as it is said (Numbers 14:17) 'and now, let the strength of YHWH grow, please'; and the wicked weaken His strength, as it is said, 'The Rock that begot you, you weakened' (Deuteronomy 32:18). And all this is said from the side of the recipients, for in truth there is no change above, as it is written (Malachi 3:6) 'I, YHWH, have not changed.' Rather, this weakening of strength is at a time when the wicked person's sins overtake him and his sentence is decreed to sever the flow of the channels from him — it appears as though there is, heaven forbid, a weakening of strength above that withholds from bestowing good upon him. But the righteous cause the flow of the channels, and through them the Attribute of above is seen." "And what was stated, 'who brought you out of the land of Egypt,' and was not stated 'who created heaven and earth' — this is because one who wishes to lie distances his witnesses, for they did not see this thing. Therefore He mentioned to them the matter that they saw with their own eyes, and so you will find in the Zohar. And 'who created you' was not stated, because our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Eruvin 13b): it would have been better for a person had he not been created than having been created, and He did not come here to mention anything but the good things that He bestowed upon them, for because of them they are obligated to serve Him."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"], 1 ["the Almighty"], 2 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:52.945255938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}